# The build context is uploaded to the build host before a single instruction runs, so
# what is excluded here is measured in minutes of transfer. `target` alone is tens of
# gigabytes once libwebrtc has been unpacked into it, and none of it is usable by the
# builder anyway — the image's target directory is a cache mount belonging to the build
# host, and a macOS-built artifact could not link into a Linux binary regardless.
/target
/node_modules
/.git

# Real call data from a checkout run. It would land in the image as a layer and read
# back as this deployment's usage history, which it is not.
/conversations.jsonl
